From de8efc5152b201d20ee4db3961ecc725f5e89106 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:17:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add a paged playlist contents command

Opening a big playlist sent every track in one message, so the first open was slow
and the listing held thousands of items it was not showing.

music/playlists/playlist_tracks_page takes limit, offset, order_by, search and the
A-Z jump bounds starts_from / starts_before. In provider order without a search or
bound it stops reading the provider as soon as the page is full; any other order, a
search or a letter bound reads everything first because the contents are not in the
database. Name orders sort on the folded name, so the list agrees with where a jump
lands. The existing playlist_tracks command is unchanged, so playback and other
clients are unaffected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
